#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:80
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:82
#, no-c-format
msgid "&krdc; lets you view and control a desktop on another computer. You can use it to work on a remote machine or help another user. The computer you connect to must run a compatible remote desktop server; &krdc; is the client and does not enable desktop sharing on that computer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid "If you want to start &krdc; from &konsole;, the command is <userinput><command>krdc</command></userinput>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid "&krdc; supports <acronym>VNC</acronym> (Virtual Network Computing), <acronym>RDP</acronym> (Remote Desktop Protocol), and <acronym>SPICE</acronym>. The protocols available in your installation depend on the installed and enabled plugins. For example, you can connect to a desktop shared by &krfb; using <acronym>VNC</acronym>, to a Remote Desktop server using <acronym>RDP</acronym>, or to a virtual machine with a <acronym>SPICE</acronym> server."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid "Please report any problems or feature requests to the &kde; mailing lists or file a bug at <ulink url=\"https://bugs.kde.org\">https://bugs.kde.org</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid "Start &krdc; from your application launcher or run <userinput><command>krdc</command></userinput> in a terminal. For command-line examples, see <xref linkend=\"command-line\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Remote Frame Buffer protocol"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid "This chapter provides a brief description of the Remote Frame Buffer protocol used by &krdc; and by other compatible systems. If you are already familiar with Remote Frame Buffer, you can safely skip this chapter."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:100
#, no-c-format
msgid "Supported Protocols"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:102
#, no-c-format
msgid "&krdc; supports <acronym>VNC</acronym>, <acronym>RDP</acronym>, and <acronym>SPICE</acronym> through protocol plugins. Select the protocol that matches the server on the remote computer. The client and server can run different operating systems."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:105
#, no-c-format
msgid "The high level implementation of a system using the Remote Frame Buffer protocol is known as Virtual Network Computer, or more often just as <acronym>VNC</acronym>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:108
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>VNC</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:110
#, no-c-format
msgid "<acronym>VNC</acronym> uses the Remote Frame Buffer (<acronym>RFB</acronym>) protocol. The server sends updates of its desktop image to the client, and the client sends keyboard and pointer input back to the server. It is commonly used to share an existing desktop session."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:111
#, no-c-format
msgid "Remote Frame Buffer (or <acronym>RFB</acronym> for short) is a simple protocol for remote access to graphical user interfaces. It works at the frame-buffer level, which roughly corresponds to the rendered screen image, which means that it can be applied to all windowing systems (including X11, &MacOS; and &Microsoft; &Windows;). Remote Frame Buffer applications exist for many platforms, and can often be free re-distributed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:115
#, no-c-format
msgid "<ulink url=\"https://apps.kde.org/krfb/\">&krfb;</ulink> is &kde;'s desktop sharing application and provides a <acronym>VNC</acronym> server for sharing a &plasma; desktop. Start and configure &krfb; on the computer whose desktop you want to share, then connect to it from &krdc; using <acronym>VNC</acronym>. Other compatible VNC servers can also be used."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:121
#, no-c-format
msgid "Connection speed and the amount of change on the remote screen affect responsiveness. If updates are slow, try a lower <acronym>VNC</acronym> quality setting in <xref linkend=\"vnc-settings\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:121
#, no-c-format
msgid "In the Remote Frame Buffer protocol, the application that runs on the machine where the user sits (containing the display, keyboard and pointer) is called the client. The application that runs on the machine where the framebuffer is located (which is running the windowing system and applications that the user is remotely controlling) is called the server. &krdc; is the &kde; client for the Remote Frame Buffer protocol. &krfb; is the &kde; server for the Remote Frame Buffer protocol."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:127
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>RDP</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid "<acronym>RDP</acronym> (Remote Desktop Protocol) provides remote access to a desktop, with features such as audio playback and clipboard exchange. Available features depend on the server and its configuration."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:132
#, no-c-format
msgid "It takes a reasonable amount of network traffic to send an image of the framebuffer, so Remote Frame Buffer works best over high bandwidth links, such as a local area network. It is still possible to use &krdc; over other links, but performance is unlikely to be as good."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:133
#, no-c-format
msgid "In &kde; &plasma;, <ulink url=\"https://invent.kde.org/plasma/krdp\"> <application>KRDP</application></ulink> provides an RDP server for sharing a Wayland desktop session. Configure remote desktop access in &plasma;'s &systemsettings;, then connect from &krdc; using <acronym>RDP</acronym>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:138
#, no-c-format
msgid "<acronym>RDP</acronym> is also used natively by &Microsoft; &Windows; Remote Desktop. You can connect to a Windows PC after enabling Remote Desktop on it. Hosting incoming connections requires a supported edition; Windows Home does not include the Remote Desktop server."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:143
#, no-c-format
msgid "For display, sound, sharing, gateway, and other connection options, see <xref linkend=\"rdp-settings\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:144
#, no-c-format
msgid "It is very easy to use &krdc; - it has a simple interface, as shown in the screenshot below."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:148
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>SPICE</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:150
#, no-c-format
msgid "<acronym>SPICE</acronym> is commonly used to access the graphical console of a virtual machine. <application>QEMU</application> can provide a SPICE server for a guest, and tools such as <application>virt-manager</application> can configure that server through <application>libvirt</application>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:155
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enable a SPICE display for the virtual machine and obtain its listening address and port from the virtualization configuration. In &krdc;, connect to the host running QEMU and the port assigned to that virtual machine. This connects to the guest's console through the virtualization host, rather than to a remote desktop server running inside the guest."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:161
#, no-c-format
msgid "The guest agent, <application>spice-vdagent</application>, enables integration features such as clipboard sharing and dynamic resolution changes. See <xref linkend=\"spice-settings\"/> for &krdc; options and the <ulink url=\"https://www.spice-space.org/spice-user-manual.html\">SPICE User Manual</ulink> for QEMU, virt-manager, and guest configuration."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:165
#, no-c-format
msgid "&krdc; is a client, and it needs to be used with compatible servers. There are different ways to connect to those servers:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:170
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using &krdc;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:172
#, no-c-format
msgid "Directly typing the server name (or IP address) into the <guilabel>Connect to:</guilabel> input."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:174
#, no-c-format
msgid "Here's a screenshot of &krdc;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:176
#, no-c-format
msgid "By using an invitation that you received. &krfb; uses invitations, and can send them by email."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:180
#, no-c-format
msgid "&krdc; main window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:181
#, no-c-format
msgid "Let's look at each of these in turn."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:185
#, no-c-format
msgid "Server name entry"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:186
#, no-c-format
msgid "If you know the host name (or IP address) of the server you want to connect to, you can enter it directly into the <guilabel>Connect to:</guilabel> input."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:187
#, no-c-format
msgid "Connecting &krdc; to compatible servers"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:189
#, no-c-format
msgid "Before connecting, enable the appropriate remote desktop server on the remote computer and obtain its address and login details. The server must be reachable from your computer, and its firewall must allow the required connection."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:191
#, no-c-format
msgid "If you want to connect to a machine named megan, which is running a <acronym>VNC</acronym> server on screen 1 (5901), you can enter <userinput>megan:1</userinput> or <userinput>megan:5901</userinput> and choose <guilabel>vnc</guilabel> as the protocol in the drop down box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:195
#, no-c-format
msgid "Choose <menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>New Connection</guimenuitem></menuchoice> to open the connection page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:197
#, no-c-format
msgid "Select <guilabel>vnc</guilabel>, <guilabel>rdp</guilabel>, or <guilabel>spice</guilabel> in the protocol selector next to <guilabel>Connect to:</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:200
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enter the server address in the form <userinput>[username@]host[:port]</userinput>, then press <keycap>Enter</keycap> or click the arrow button next to the address. The protocol is already selected, so do not prepend it to this field."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:204
#, no-c-format
msgid "Review the host settings if prompted, and enter the credentials required by the server. Each connection opens in a tab."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: acronym
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:209
#, no-c-format
msgid "<acronym>VNC</acronym>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:210
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enter <userinput>megan</userinput> for the default port 5900. For display 1 on port 5901, enter <userinput>megan:1</userinput> or <userinput>megan:5901</userinput>. Port numbers below 100 are interpreted as <acronym>VNC</acronym> display numbers and added to 5900."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:212
#, no-c-format
msgid "Similary, if you are using a <acronym>RDP</acronym> server on that machine, you can enter <userinput>megan</userinput>. Choose <guilabel>rdp</guilabel> as the protocol. <acronym>RDP</acronym> does not need the screen number to be specified. If the server runs the <acronym>RDP</acronym> server not on the default port, you may specify it in the following way: <userinput>megan:3910</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:217
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Entering a hostname into &krdc;</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:219
#, no-c-format
msgid "You need to enter an &URL; in percent encoded syntax, i.e. @ as %40, for &eg; <userinput>username%40ad.domain.example</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:223
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Entering a hostname into &krdc;</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:226
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using an invitation"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:227
#, no-c-format
msgid "Within the &krfb; server application, it is possible to send invitations over email (and in other ways, although email is the most useful). If you receive this type of email invitation, you can just click on the link provided in the mail. This will start &krdc; if it is not already running, and connect to the server specified in the invitation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: acronym
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:228
#, no-c-format
msgid "<acronym>RDP</acronym>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:518
#, no-c-format
msgid "Why does <acronym>RDP</acronym> support not work?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:229
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enter <userinput>megan</userinput> for the default port 3389, or <userinput>megan:3390</userinput> for a different port. You can include a user name, for example <userinput>alice@megan</userinput>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: acronym
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:232
#, no-c-format
msgid "<acronym>SPICE</acronym>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:233
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enter the host and port of the virtual machine's <acronym>SPICE</acronym> server, for example <userinput>vmhost:5902</userinput>. The default port is 5900."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:238
#, no-c-format
msgid "The connection page also lists bookmarks, connection history, and <acronym>VNC</acronym> services advertised on the local network through Zeroconf. Typing in the address field filters this list. You can select a listed connection and use <guimenuitem>Connect</guimenuitem> from its context menu. The <guilabel>Remote Desktops</guilabel> panel provides another way to find saved and discovered connections."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:242
#, no-c-format
msgid "Notice: Before connecting, ensure that the target computer (server) is available on the network and, if necessary, that its firewall has been correctly configured or disabled."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:247
#, no-c-format
msgid "What happens when you connect"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:248
#, no-c-format
msgid "No matter how you select the server to connect to, the next thing that happens is that &krdc; asks you about the network connection to the server, as shown below:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:249
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guilabel>Host Configuration</guilabel> dialog contains settings for the selected protocol. Clear <guilabel>Show this dialog again for this host</guilabel> to reuse them without being prompted on each connection. Settings are associated with the connection address; connecting by a different host name or IP address can use a different configuration."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:257
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>&krdc; connection speed selection</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:354
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>&krdc; full screen mode selection</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:368
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>&krdc; window mode selection</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:263
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>&krdc; connection speed selection</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:268
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are three speed settings for the <acronym>VNC</acronym> protocol:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:360
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>&krdc; full screen mode selection</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:374
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>&krdc; window mode selection</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:269
#, no-c-format
msgid "When the server requests authentication, enter your password and, if requested, your user name. The <guilabel>Remember password</guilabel> option allows &krdc; to store credentials through the system credential store using QtKeychain. Password storage also depends on the global <guilabel>Remember passwords</guilabel> setting."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:273
#, no-c-format
msgid "High Quality (LAN, direct connection), which is the default, and you should evaluate how well this setting performs before selecting a lower performance option that uses less bandwidth."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:277
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>&krdc; password entry</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:277
#, no-c-format
msgid "Medium Quality (DSL, Cable, fast Internet)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:279
#, no-c-format
msgid "Low Quality (Modem, ISDN, slow Internet)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:283
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>&krdc; password entry</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:283
#, no-c-format
msgid "If you always operate over the same link type, you can deselect the checkbox labeled <guilabel>Show this dialog again for this host</guilabel>, which means that you won't be asked about the connection type again for this host, providing you identify it in the same way. For example, if a host has two names, and deselect the checkbox when connecting using one name, you won't get asked if you connect using that name, although you will be asked if you use the other name, or the IP address."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:289
#, no-c-format
msgid "For <acronym>RDP</acronym>, &krdc; may ask you to verify an unknown or changed server certificate. Check the certificate details with the server administrator before accepting it. The dialog offers <guilabel>Remember this certificate</guilabel> for subsequent connections."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:294
#, no-c-format
msgid "The tab icon indicates connection status. After authentication succeeds, you can view or control the remote desktop."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:294
#, no-c-format
msgid "You select the appropriate speed setting, and select the <guibutton>OK</guibutton> to proceed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:299
#, no-c-format
msgid "Controlling the remote desktop connection"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:299
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can see the connection status in the icon in the tab."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:301
#, no-c-format
msgid "Use the keyboard and mouse in a connected tab to work on the remote desktop. The toolbar shown below provides controls for opening connections, changing the view, and interacting with the remote desktop. Buttons may be unavailable depending on the protocol and connection state."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:303
#, no-c-format
msgid "Depending on the configuration of the server, you may (and almost certainly will) need to provide a password to authenticate to the server. &krdc; will provide a password dialog similar to that shown below."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:308
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>&krdc; toolbar</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:310
#, no-c-format
msgid "&krdc; has the ability to save the password for further connections to the same host. It uses KWallet for doing this. You need to check the <guibutton>Remember password (KWallet)</guibutton> check box if you like to use this feature."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:314
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>&krdc; toolbar</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:320
#, no-c-format
msgid "From left to right, the toolbar contains the following buttons:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:324
#, no-c-format
msgid "New Connection"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:325
#, no-c-format
msgid "Open the connection page to choose a protocol and enter a server address. The new connection opens in a tab, so you can keep other sessions open."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:329
#, no-c-format
msgid "Full Screen"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:330
#, no-c-format
msgid "Display the remote desktop in full screen. The button changes to <guibutton>Window Mode</guibutton>, which returns to the normal window. In full screen, use the floating toolbar to access session controls. <guimenuitem>Stick Toolbar</guimenuitem> keeps it visible, and <guimenuitem>Minimize Full Screen Window</guimenuitem> gives access to your local desktop."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:331
#, no-c-format
msgid "After authentication, you will be connected to the remote server, and can begin using &krdc; to observe or control the remote desktop."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:337
#, no-c-format
msgid "Screenshot"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:338
#, no-c-format
msgid "Copy an image of the remote desktop to the local clipboard. Paste it into an image editor or another application to save it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:340
#, no-c-format
msgid "Having connected to the remote server, you would normally use the keyboard and mouse to control the windowing system and applications on that remote machine."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:342
#, no-c-format
msgid "View Only"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:343
#, no-c-format
msgid "Observe the remote desktop without sending keyboard or mouse input. Clipboard sharing is also suppressed while this option is enabled. Click the button again to resume controlling the remote desktop."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:346
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can view the remote desktop either as a full screen, or as a window on the local desktop. You can change between these modes using icons shown below."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:348
#, no-c-format
msgid "Clipboard Sharing"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:349
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enable or disable clipboard exchange between your computer and the remote desktop. Supported content depends on the protocol and server. Clipboard exchange requires <guibutton>View Only</guibutton> to be turned off."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:354
#, no-c-format
msgid "Local Cursor"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:355
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show a local mouse pointer to help track its position over the remote desktop. Click the button again to turn this option off."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:359
#, no-c-format
msgid "Grab Keys"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:360
#, no-c-format
msgid "Send as many keyboard shortcuts as possible to the remote desktop. Some shortcuts may remain reserved by the local desktop or window system. Turn this option off to handle shortcuts locally again. Automatic keyboard grabbing on entering full screen can be enabled in the general settings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:366
#, no-c-format
msgid "Scale"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:367
#, no-c-format
msgid "Scale the remote image to fit the available window area. Turn this option off to view the desktop without scaling. &krdc; remembers separate scaling choices for window and full screen modes. This changes the displayed image size, rather than the remote desktop resolution."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:373
#, no-c-format
msgid "Disconnect"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:374
#, no-c-format
msgid "Close the current connection. Closing its tab also disconnects it. This does not issue a logout or shutdown command to the remote computer; what happens to the remote session depends on the server."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:380
#, no-c-format
msgid "Full screen mode is normally better when you are helping a remote user, because you can see all of what they can see. Window mode is most useful when you are working both remotely and locally - perhaps referring to some local documentation and then using those instructions on the remote machine."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:382
#, no-c-format
msgid "Bookmarks and connection history"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:384
#, no-c-format
msgid "To save a connection, choose <menuchoice><guimenu>Bookmarks</guimenu><guimenuitem>Add Bookmark</guimenuitem></menuchoice>. Open it again from the <guimenu>Bookmarks</guimenu> menu or the connection list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:388
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using window mode"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:390
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>&krdc; bookmarks menu</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:390
#, no-c-format
msgid "In window mode, you can terminate the connection by closing the window, by clicking on the logout button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:396
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>&krdc; bookmarks menu</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:397
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using full screen mode"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:399
#, no-c-format
msgid "In full screen mode, you can change the appearance of the toolbar. The transparency of the toolbar can be changed with scrollwheel."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:402
#, no-c-format
msgid "When <guilabel>Remember connection history</guilabel> is enabled, successful connections are recorded under <menuchoice><guimenu>Bookmarks</guimenu><guimenuitem>History</guimenuitem></menuchoice> and appear in the connection list. Right-click a saved entry in the list to connect, rename it, change its settings, or delete it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:408
#, no-c-format
msgid "For a bookmarked connection, the settings dialog can also edit its <guilabel>Name:</guilabel> and <guilabel>URL:</guilabel>. Use a complete URL such as <userinput>rdp://alice@megan:3389</userinput>, keeping the same protocol. Changes to connection settings may take effect only when you reconnect."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:408
#, no-c-format
msgid "Bookmarks"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:410
#, no-c-format
msgid "&krdc; has the ability to manage bookmarks. If you need to connect often to the same remote desktop, you can add an entry for this connection to the bookmark list. You can do so with a click on <menuchoice><guimenu>Bookmarks</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Add Bookmark</guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:415
#, no-c-format
msgid "Managing &krdc; configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:417
#, no-c-format
msgid "Open <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure KRDC...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> to change application preferences."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:447
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure KRDC...</guimenuitem></menuchoice>, you can open a dialog to modify the behavior of &krdc;. Selecting that button brings up a window as shown below:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:422
#, no-c-format
msgid "&krdc; preferences - General tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:428
#, no-c-format
msgid "&krdc; preferences - <guilabel>General</guilabel> tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:432
#, no-c-format
msgid "History Bookmarks"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:434
#, no-c-format
msgid "&krdc; saves last used remote desktop connections. You can access these special bookmarks at <menuchoice><guimenu>Bookmarks</guimenu><guimenuitem>History</guimenuitem></menuchoice>. Of course you can also delete a bookmark of this list if you don't need it anymore in the list. Just click <guibutton>Delete Bookmark</guibutton> which appears after a click with the right mouse button on the bookmark you would like to delete."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:484
#, no-c-format
msgid "&krdc; preferences - <guilabel>RDP Defaults</guilabel> tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:435
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>General</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:436
#, no-c-format
msgid "Choose whether to restore open sessions on startup, remember history and passwords, display a system tray icon or status bar, and preserve the aspect ratio when scaling. You can also configure the default protocol, initial host configuration dialog, window resizing, automatic full screen and keyboard grabbing, and tab appearance and closing behavior."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:441
#, no-c-format
msgid "Hosts"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:442
#, no-c-format
msgid "Select a saved host and click <guibutton>Configure...</guibutton> to change its protocol settings. <guibutton>Remove</guibutton> deletes the saved host configuration. Bookmarks and connection history are managed separately."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:446
#, no-c-format
msgid "Plugins"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:447
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enable or disable installed protocol plugins. Restart &krdc; after changing plugin availability. The configuration button of a protocol plugin opens its default settings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:454
#, no-c-format
msgid "VNC settings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:458
#, no-c-format
msgid "&krdc; preferences - <guilabel>VNC</guilabel> tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:469
#, no-c-format
msgid "&krdc; preferences - <guilabel>VNC Defaults</guilabel> tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:464
#, no-c-format
msgid "&krdc; preferences - <guilabel>VNC</guilabel> profiles tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:475
#, no-c-format
msgid "&krdc; preferences - <guilabel>VNC Defaults</guilabel> profiles tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:470
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Connection type:</guilabel> offers <guilabel>High Quality (LAN, direct connection)</guilabel>, <guilabel>Medium Quality (DSL, Cable, fast Internet)</guilabel>, and <guilabel>Low Quality (Modem, ISDN, slow Internet)</guilabel>. Choose a quality appropriate to the whole connection, including the remote computer's network link. A lower quality can help on slow connections."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:477
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Scale to Size:</guilabel> sets the size used to display the remote desktop, with predefined and custom dimensions. The password-manager option prevents sending clipboard content marked as a password by supported password managers, such as KeePassXC. It cannot identify passwords copied by applications that do not provide that marker."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:485
#, no-c-format
msgid "RDP settings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:487
#, no-c-format
msgid "The RDP configuration dialog contains the following tabs. Changes to connection settings may take effect only after reconnecting."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:490
#, no-c-format
msgid "<emphasis role=\"bold\">General</emphasis>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:494
#, no-c-format
msgid "&krdc; RDP preferences - General tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:500
#, no-c-format
msgid "&krdc; preferences - <guilabel>RDP</guilabel> general tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:506
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guilabel>General</guilabel> tab controls the appearance of the remote desktop, input devices, and resources shared with the remote session."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:509
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Resolution</guilabel> selects the desktop size requested from the server. Choose a preset, the current window or screen size, or a custom width and height. <guilabel>Use All Screens Resolution</guilabel> requests a multi-monitor session; in full screen, the remote monitors are displayed on the corresponding local screens. Availability depends on the server and your local display configuration."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:516
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Scale window contents to match resolution</guilabel> controls local image scaling. <guilabel>Desktop scale factor:</guilabel> and <guilabel>Device scale factor:</guilabel> instead specify scaling information sent to the server. Use these to adjust the size of remote interface elements on high-resolution displays, where supported by the server."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:521
#, no-c-format
msgid "<acronym>RDP</acronym> support in &krdc; depends on xfreerdp (FreeRDP). Make sure that you have installed this runtime dependency."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:522
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Acceleration:</guilabel> selects the graphics encoding mode, including H.264, RemoteFX, or disabling acceleration. <guilabel>Color depth:</guilabel> controls the number of colors used for the remote desktop; some acceleration modes require 32-bit color. <guilabel>Keyboard layout:</guilabel> should match the keyboard you use so that key presses are interpreted correctly."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:529
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Sound:</guilabel> selects playback on this computer, playback on the remote computer, or no sound. <guilabel>Share Media:</guilabel> makes a local directory available to the remote session; leave it empty to disable drive sharing. <guilabel>Share Smartcard:</guilabel> specifies the smartcard name to redirect to the server."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:535
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Admin (or console) session</guilabel> requests an administrative session on servers that support it. <guilabel>Prevent remote session lock</guilabel> sends periodic simulated mouse activity to keep the session active; server policies may still enforce locking."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:540
#, no-c-format
msgid "Security"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:544
#, no-c-format
msgid "&krdc; RDP preferences - Security tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:550
#, no-c-format
msgid "&krdc; preferences - <guilabel>RDP</guilabel> security tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:556
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guilabel>Security</guilabel> tab controls which security methods &krdc; offers when establishing the RDP connection. The <guilabel>NLA</guilabel>, <guilabel>TLS</guilabel>, <guilabel>RDP</guilabel>, and <guilabel>Ext</guilabel> check boxes enable the corresponding FreeRDP security modes. More than one can be enabled so that the client and server can negotiate a compatible method."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:563
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>TLS security level:</guilabel> sets the cryptographic security level required for TLS connections. A higher level imposes stricter requirements and may prevent connections to older servers."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:567
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Authentication Package List:</guilabel> passes a custom selection of authentication packages to FreeRDP. Leave it empty to use the default behavior, or enter the value supplied by your administrator. Change security options to match the server's requirements."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:572
#, no-c-format
msgid "Proxy"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:576
#, no-c-format
msgid "&krdc; RDP preferences - Proxy tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:582
#, no-c-format
msgid "&krdc; preferences - <guilabel>RDP</guilabel> proxy tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:588
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guilabel>Proxy</guilabel> tab configures a network proxy used for the connection. Select <guilabel>HTTP</guilabel> or <guilabel>SOCKS</guilabel> in <guilabel>Protocol:</guilabel>, then enter the proxy address in <guilabel>Server:</guilabel> using the form <userinput>host:port</userinput>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:593
#, no-c-format
msgid "If the proxy requires authentication, fill in <guilabel>Username:</guilabel> and <guilabel>Password:</guilabel> with the proxy credentials. These may differ from the credentials for the remote desktop. Leave <guilabel>Server:</guilabel> empty when no proxy is needed. The target remote desktop address remains the address entered on the connection page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:599
#, no-c-format
msgid "Gateway"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:603
#, no-c-format
msgid "&krdc; RDP preferences - Gateway tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:609
#, no-c-format
msgid "&krdc; preferences - <guilabel>RDP</guilabel> gateway tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:615
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guilabel>Gateway</guilabel> tab configures access through an RDP gateway, which provides a route to a remote desktop on another network. Enter the gateway address in <guilabel>Server:</guilabel> as <userinput>host:port</userinput>, using the port supplied by your administrator. Keep the destination computer's address on the main connection page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:621
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enter the gateway account's <guilabel>Domain:</guilabel>, <guilabel>Username:</guilabel>, and <guilabel>Password:</guilabel> as required. These fields authenticate access to the gateway; the remote desktop may require separate credentials."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:626
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Transport type:</guilabel> offers <guilabel>Auto</guilabel>, <guilabel>HTTP</guilabel>, and <guilabel>RPC</guilabel>. Use <guilabel>Auto</guilabel> unless your administrator specifies a transport. Leave the gateway <guilabel>Server:</guilabel> field empty when connecting without an RDP gateway."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:632
#, no-c-format
msgid "If SSH tunnel support is available, an additional <guilabel>SSH tunnel</guilabel> tab appears in the host configuration dialog. See <xref linkend=\"ssh-tunnels\"/> for its options."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:638
#, no-c-format
msgid "SPICE settings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:642
#, no-c-format
msgid "&krdc; preferences - <guilabel>SPICE</guilabel> tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:648
#, no-c-format
msgid "&krdc; preferences - <guilabel>SPICE</guilabel> profiles tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:490
#, no-c-format
msgid "&krdc; preferences - <guilabel>RDP Defaults</guilabel> profiles tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:654
#, no-c-format
msgid "Choose the requested remote resolution from the presets, the current window or screen size, or custom dimensions. Dynamic resizing requires <application>spice-vdagent</application> in the guest. You can also enable local scaling and audio playback. Clipboard exchange depends on support in the guest."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:661
#, no-c-format
msgid "SSH tunnels"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:665
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>&krdc; preferences - <guilabel>SSH</guilabel> tab</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:671
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>&krdc; preferences - <guilabel>SSH</guilabel> tab</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:677
#, no-c-format
msgid "If your installation includes SSH tunnel support, the host settings offer <guilabel>Connect via SSH tunnel</guilabel>. Enter the SSH port and user name for the same host as the remote desktop server. SSH authentication is separate from remote desktop authentication."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:682
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Tunnel via loopback address</guilabel> makes the tunnel connect to the remote desktop service through the remote host's loopback address. Use this when the service listens only on that address. The remote desktop port still comes from the connection address."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:690
#, no-c-format
msgid "Starting connections from the command line"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:691
#, no-c-format
msgid "Pass a complete URL to connect directly:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:692
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput><command>krdc</command> rdp://alice@megan</userinput>\n"
"<userinput><command>krdc</command> vnc://megan:5901</userinput>\n"
"<userinput><command>krdc</command> spice://vmhost:5902</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:694
#, no-c-format
msgid "Use <option>--fullscreen</option> with one URL to start that connection in full screen. You can also pass several URLs to open multiple connections:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:696
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput><command>krdc</command> --fullscreen rdp://megan</userinput>\n"
"<userinput><command>krdc</command> vnc://megan rdp://workstation</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:698
#, no-c-format
msgid "In a complete URL, percent-encode reserved characters in the user name. For example, use <userinput>rdp://alice%40example.org@megan</userinput> for the user name <literal>alice@example.org</literal>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:702
#, no-c-format
msgid "&krdc; can read basic connection details from an <filename>.rdp</filename> file passed on the command line:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:704
#, no-c-format
msgid "<userinput><command>krdc</command> connection.rdp</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:705
#, no-c-format
msgid "This reads the server address, user name, domain, and a password field if present; it does not import every setting supported by other RDP clients. Use the host configuration dialog for other options. Run <userinput><command>krdc</command> <option>--help</option></userinput> for command-line help."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:714
#, no-c-format
msgid "Questions and Answers"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:717
#, no-c-format
msgid "Why is a protocol missing or an address rejected?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:718
#, no-c-format
msgid "Check that the corresponding plugin is installed and enabled in <guilabel>Plugins</guilabel>, then restart &krdc;. Check the selected protocol and address syntax in <xref linkend=\"compatible-versions\"/>. RDP support uses the FreeRDP libraries directly; it does not require launching an external <command>xfreerdp</command> executable."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:725
#, no-c-format
msgid "Why can I not connect to the remote computer?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:726
#, no-c-format
msgid "Check the host name, port, network or VPN connection, and whether the remote desktop server is running. Ensure its firewall permits the connection. For authentication failures, check your user name, password, domain, and permission to log in remotely. If you use a proxy, gateway, or SSH tunnel, check its settings and credentials too."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:733
#, no-c-format
msgid "Why can I see the desktop but not control it?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:734
#, no-c-format
msgid "Turn off <guimenuitem>View Only</guimenuitem> in the <guimenu>Session</guimenu> menu. The server may also restrict your connection to viewing; ask the person administering the remote desktop to check its permissions."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:740
#, no-c-format
msgid "Why does copying and pasting not work?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:741
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enable <guimenuitem>Clipboard Sharing</guimenuitem>, disable <guimenuitem>View Only</guimenuitem>, and check that the server supports the content you are copying. For VNC, the password-manager filter can deliberately block copied passwords. For SPICE, check the guest agent."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:747
#, no-c-format
msgid "How can I change settings after hiding the host dialog?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:748
#, no-c-format
msgid "Open <guilabel>Hosts</guilabel> in the application preferences, select the host, and click <guibutton>Configure...</guibutton>. You can enable <guilabel>Show this dialog again for this host</guilabel> there."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:753
#, no-c-format
msgid "Where can I report a problem?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:754
#, no-c-format
msgid "Report bugs at <ulink url=\"https://bugs.kde.org\">the &kde; bug tracker</ulink>. Include your &krdc; version, protocol, local operating system, server software, and steps to reproduce the problem. Omit passwords and other private connection details."
msgstr ""

